      en: "Xiuguluan River, at 104 km, is the longest river in eastern Taiwan. It originates in the Zhongyang Range and flows through Hualien to the Ruisui Plain, then into the Pacific Ocean. Its watershed covers 1790 km². Known for whitewater rafting in Xiuguluan Gorge. Rafting season is April to October. The river passes through the Ruisui Hot Springs area. Culturally, it is home to Amis and Bunun indigenous people. It is a key habitat for the Formosan salmon. Average current speed is 3 m/s.",
