      en: "Basianshan Forest area in southeastern Hsinchu County, Taiwan, is part of the Basianshan National Forest Recreation Area. Known for its hot springs developed during the Japanese colonial period. The region includes Basianshan Peak (2148 m) and Jinshui Hot Springs. The forest consists of mixed forests with Taiwan red cypress, bamboo, and ferns. The area offers hiking trails, a visitor center, and a historic villa. Hot spring temperature is 48 °C. The park is a key recreational area for Hsinchu residents. Annual visitors are about 500,000.",
